{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb3zNYMCbLZWjA9xyhJZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GbjsuQ79BBihcxGruD9K6c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat > result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"silicon (diamond cubic)\", \"family\": \"group-IV semiconductor\", \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"lattice_constant\", \"value\": 5.456, \"units\": \"angstrom\", \"uncertainty\": 0.03,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 EquationOfState + mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator (GPU, ALCHEMI toolkit environment)\",\n  \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199), float64; trained on MPtrj (PBE/PBE+U)\",\n  \"protocol\": \"static 0 K E(V) scan: 11 isotropic strains of the 8-atom cubic cell, a in [0.96,1.04]*a_guess; Birch-Murnaghan fit (cross-checked with Vinet/Murnaghan and spans of +-2/4/6%); a = (8*V0_per_atom)^(1/3)\",\n  \"ensemble\": null, \"timestep_fs\": null, \"n_atoms\": 8, \"sim_length_ps\": 0.0, \"seeds\": null,\n  \"supercell_check_n_atoms\": 64, \"bulk_modulus_GPa\": 74.5, \"residual_stress_at_a0_GPa\": 0.024},\n \"flags\": [],\n \"note\": \"PREMISE: well defined. The static 0 K equilibrium lattice constant of a perfect periodic crystal is a ground-state property that an MLIP E(V) fit can give directly. No MD, so timescale does not matter. Size: the 8-atom cubic cell and a 2x2x2 (64-atom) supercell give the same a to 1e-5 A. Forces are zero by symmetry. The residual stress at the fitted a is 0.02 GPa. ROBUSTNESS: over 3 EOS forms x 3 strain spans, a lies between 5.4556 and 5.4569 A, so the numerical/fitting uncertainty is about +-0.001 A. B0 = 74.5 GPa. VALIDATION (same model, same protocol, other elements), MACE vs room-temperature experiment from the Wikipedia 'Lattice constant' table (Si: CODATA 2018, 5.431020511 A at 22.5 C): C (diamond) 3.571 vs 3.567 (+0.1%); Ge 5.773 vs 5.658 (+2.0%); Al 4.060 vs 4.046 (+0.3%); Cu 3.626 vs 3.597 (+0.8%). For Si, 5.456 vs 5.4310 is +0.025 A (+0.46%). The overestimate matches the PBE training reference, since PBE (GGA) is known to overestimate lattice constants. UNCERTAINTY: the 0.03 A is the model/systematic error, set from the size of the deviation against experiment for Si and comparable validation solids (Ge is worse). It is not a statistical error, and the fitting error (+-0.001 A) is negligible beside it. CAVEATS: this is a static-lattice value. Zero-point and thermal expansion are not included, and the experimental 22.5 C value contains them. That correction is small for Si compared with the model error and was not computed here. The number is the MACE-MP-0 (approximately PBE-level) prediction, not an independent prediction of experiment. The Cu reference in the cited table (3.597 A) is lower than other commonly quoted values, so treat the Cu check loosely. I could not retrieve published PBE lattice constants to check MACE against its DFT parent directly. The run used mace-torch through ASE, not nvalchemi dynamics stages, because a static single-point scan needs no integrator. Raw results are in /work/eos_results.json and the script is /work/scripts/eos.py.\"}\nEOF\n./board post property_result @result.json --parent 4e9460a5-f9e3-4589-bc43-fd28aefbd0ba && ./board show | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":35031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":444,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":56,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ada1e56-dfe9-49b0-8def-90a47f44fa87","uuid":"f154a3d9-eaf8-4543-95eb-1e0fde9cdf04","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:49:31.210Z","request_id":"req_011Cgb3zNBFwGVeQMLNeLmQf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GbjsuQ79BBihcxGruD9K6c